      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Verso",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>Harm has befallen all the communities because of&nbsp;</li>\n<li>his wrongdoing. Even the Christians have had wrongdoing perpetrated against them&nbsp;</li>\n<li>because of him, and [considerable] harm has come to them.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>&ndash;5. Since the day when the minbars were destroyed, the three communities have been forced to pay in fiscal penalties more than f[our]&nbsp;</li>\n<li></li>\n<li>thou[s]and dinars, and they do not kno[w]&nbsp;</li>\n<li>to whom it is given nor how much. And there is no&nbsp;</li>\n<li>&ndash;9. gain from the penalties collected by him, other than that we are exposed to public view. We are unable to count up&nbsp;</li>\n<li></li>\n<li>all his harmful acts but rather to give only a brief summary of&nbsp;</li>\n<li>&ndash;13. the matter. We have already perished and died, and our souls and money have [van]ish[ed]. Our concern and aim, for the sake of God, is the [improvement of the]&nbsp;</li>\n<li></li>\n<li></li>\n<li>situation of your sl(aves) and his dismissal from [the headship]&nbsp;</li>\n<li>and the restoration of their venerable head to them.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>We subjects are m[iserab]le, broke[n]&nbsp;</li>\n<li>&ndash;18. hearted, and poor. Your slaves have informed you about this, intending that [the] q\u0101\u1e0d\u012b,&nbsp;</li>\n<li></li>\n<li>may God honour him, would indicate to them wha[t]&nbsp;</li>\n<li>he will do, out of his bounty and for the sake of God the exalted,&nbsp;</li>\n<li>so that this wrongdoing may be re[m]oved from them,&nbsp;</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
        "sc:supplementing",
        "translating"
      ],
      "schema:position": 1
    },
